# Model Training Rules

Use PyTorch (env `mi_torch`). See `docs/MODEL_PLAN.md`.

## Baseline models (Stage 2)

- EEGNet
- DeepConvNet
- FBCNet

A reference FBCNet/EEGNet/DeepConvNet implementation by the dataset authors lives
at `/share/workspace2/moto_imagination/WBCIC_SHU/code/Deep_learning/` (READ-ONLY,
old MNE 0.22 / torch 1.10 API). Use it only as a cross-check; reimplement cleanly
for modern PyTorch rather than importing it.

## First main model (Stage 3+)

A confidence-aware multi-subagent encoder (see `docs/MODEL_PLAN.md`):
- EEGNet-style encoder backbone.
- Classification head.
- Prototype memory / head (global + subject + session prototypes).
- Confidence head (multi-source, NOT just softmax max prob).
- Optional adapter for target-subject fine-tuning and online adaptation.

## Tensor convention

- Dataset returns `X` as `[channels, time]`, `y` scalar.
- DataLoader batches `X` as `[batch, channels, time]`.
- The model adds the singleton channel dim `[batch, 1, channels, time]` internally
  if its first layer needs it. Do this conversion in the model, not the dataset.

## Losses

- Classification: `CrossEntropyLoss`.
- Prototype: pull features to the correct-class prototype, push from wrong-class.
- Confidence/calibration: confidence should correlate with correctness.
- Optional consistency loss for augmented EEG inputs.
- Optional domain (subject/session) adversarial / invariance loss.

## Training requirements

- Use fixed random seeds; record the seed in the run metadata.
- For every run save: resolved config, split file, checkpoint(s), metrics, and logs,
  all under a unique `run_id` directory in `outputs/` (and `checkpoints/`).
- Never overwrite an existing run's results without an explicit new `run_id`.
- Report Accuracy, Balanced Accuracy, and Macro-F1 at minimum.
- For confidence models also report ECE, NLL, Brier score, and a risk-coverage
  curve when implemented.
- Expose all key hyperparameters through YAML configs in `configs/`; scripts read
  the config path via `argparse`. No hardcoded hyperparameters in scripts.
- GPU training must run via Slurm `sbatch`, never on the login node.
